<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">La Mosquitia</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">La <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosquito-coast">Mosquitia</a> is a sparsely populated region of rainforest, pine savanna and lagoons in eastern Honduras, the Honduran part of the Mosquito Coast that extends into Nicaragua. It is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/miskito">Miskito</a> and other indigenous peoples, and from the seventeenth to the nineteenth century it was under British influence through the Miskito kingdom. Its Río Plátano Biosphere Reserve is a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/la-mosquitia.jpg" alt="La Mosquitia" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mapa Miskito.png: DaDez~commonswiki (talk · contribs) NIcaraguaGeneralV2.svg: Rowanwindwhistler (talk · contribs) der... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mapa_Miskito-es.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
